<h2>🔗 10. Coupling and uncoupling a semi-trailer</h2>
<p>A safe operation means securing the combination, following the manufacturer's procedure and visually confirming that the fifth wheel is locked.</p>
<h3>Coupling: essential steps</h3>
<ol>
<li>Park the tractor unit and semi-trailer on firm, preferably level ground. Apply the parking brakes and make sure the trailer is stable.</li>
<li>Check trailer height and fifth-wheel position according to the manual. Inspect the fifth wheel, kingpin and coupling area.</li>
<li>Align the tractor unit slowly. Reverse carefully until the kingpin engages correctly with the fifth wheel. Keep everyone clear of the space between the vehicles.</li>
<li>Carry out the manufacturer's locking check: a gentle tug test and a safe visual check of the locking mechanism. Stop if anything is uncertain.</li>
<li>Connect the air and electrical lines correctly. Check for damage or crossed connections and secure them in their holders.</li>
<li>Raise the landing legs fully, check brakes, lights and connections, then walk around the combination for a final inspection.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Uncoupling: essential steps</h3>
<ol>
<li>Choose firm, level ground. Secure the combination with the brakes and prevent the trailer from moving.</li>
<li>Lower the landing legs until they firmly support the trailer, following the equipment instructions.</li>
<li>With the vehicle secured, disconnect the electrical and air lines and stow them safely in their holders.</li>
<li>Release the fifth-wheel locking mechanism as instructed by the manufacturer. Never go underneath a trailer that is not safely supported.</li>
<li>Move the tractor unit forward slowly and confirm that the trailer remains stable on its landing legs.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Common errors to avoid:</strong> driving away without confirming kingpin lock; forgetting connections or landing legs; releasing the fifth wheel before supporting the trailer; standing between vehicles during a manoeuvre; continuing when the coupling looks incorrect.</p>
<p><strong>Important:</strong> this is educational guidance. Controls, fifth-wheel designs and procedures vary. Always follow the manufacturer's manual, company procedures and supervised practical training.</p>
<p><strong>Manufacturer visual references:</strong> <a href="https://safholland.com/us/en/service/download-center/document/resource/environment/project1_p/documents/documentationP/2026/2026_01/XL-FW20231UM-en-US%2520Rev-_web.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SAF-HOLLAND illustrated coupling manual</a> · <a href="https://vimeopro.com/safholland/service-operational" target="_blank" rel="noopener">step-by-step coupling and uncoupling videos</a>.</p>
